WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:08.340
SCP-049 was many things: a doctor, an enemy
of The Pestilence, a seemingly immortal masked

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:15.320
anomaly contained by the SCP Foundation, but
above all else, he was a scholar, a man in

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.910
constant pursuit of knowledge.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:22.630
Whether he was conducting whatever experiments
he could get away with in containment, reading

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:27.630
the various medical texts he was allowed upon
request, or asking questions of his fellow

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:33.380
anomalies as they passed by his cell, he was
always looking for new information and additional

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.290
subjects of study.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.700
Sometimes they pertained to the Pestilence,
but other times they were simply things that

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:44.399
he engaged with for the pure joy of discovery
and understanding.

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:49.610
After a bout of particularly impressive good
behavior, namely a willingness to cooperate

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:54.239
with questions from researchers and a record-breaking
streak of days without any reanimation of

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:59.920
deceased tissue, the Plague Doctor was given
the exciting opportunity to peruse a selection

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.010
of official SCP files.

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:07.640
Any potentially compromising information was
heavily redacted, of course, but the Doctor

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.799
was nevertheless thrilled at the chance.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:15.670
He greedily devoured file after file while
sipping a cup of hot tea, poring over reports

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.700
of invisible women and supernatural vending
machines.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:24.200
Finally, he came to the file for SCP-2935.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:29.259
As the Doctor read about the space-time anomaly
in a cave in Indiana, holding the gateway

00:01:29.259 --> 00:01:35.970
to another reality where all life mysteriously
ended, his mind began to race with possibilities.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:41.560
What could have wiped out everything so efficiently,
in such a perfect, horrible swoop, on the

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.040
date of April 20, 2016?

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:49.250
He could think of only one explanation, and
he began to obsess.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:54.540
After days of rereading the file again and
again, the Plague Doctor could take no more.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:59.991
He requested an audience with a Senior Researcher,
and was granted a meeting with Sr. Researcher

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:00.991
Sun.

00:02:00.991 --> 00:02:02.860
"What did you want to ask me about?"

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:03.969
Dr. Sun inquired.

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:08.679
"Please, Doctor...You must understand, there
is so little I can do to continue my work

00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:10.250
in my current state.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:15.370
Meanwhile, the Pestilence rages on outside
of these walls, at times even within them,

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:16.370
and I can do nothing.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.370
But this!"

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.080
He held up the file for SCP-2935.

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.060
"This may hold the key to all that I seek.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:30.090
I only ask that you permit me to venture inside
on a research expedition of my own."

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.750
"You want to go...into SCP-2935?"

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:39.630
Dr. Sun had prepared herself for a lot of
possible requests, but this was not one of

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:40.630
them.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.390
"Yes, Doctor, I do."

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.730
"And...you understand what that would mean?"

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:50.740
Dr. Sun studied the Plague Doctor's face,
but the mask revealed no expression but stony

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:51.740
determination.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:56.370
"You wouldn't be able to come back, you would
have to stay there, indefinitely."

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.700
"I understand.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.349
That is a sacrifice I am fully prepared to
make.

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:02.819
Out of one prison and into another, yes?

00:03:02.819 --> 00:03:06.129
But there, I will have so much to study.

00:03:06.129 --> 00:03:07.330
So much to learn.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:11.030
Perhaps, I will at last find the answers I
seek."

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:12.420
Dr. Sun nodded.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.510
"Let me speak to the higher-ups about this.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.900
I'll see what they have to say."

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.150
The Plague Doctor waited patiently in his
cell, thinking of nothing but the verdict

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:23.620
that awaited him, until finally Dr. Sun returned.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:24.690
"Yes, Doctor?

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.290
What is it?"

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.310
"Your request has been approved."

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.269
Dr. Sun sounded almost surprised.

00:03:30.269 --> 00:03:32.880
"We'll get you transported to Indiana tomorrow."

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:35.460
"Then I suppose I must bid you adieu, Doctor."

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:38.330
The Plague Doctor nodded solemnly.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:39.330
"Goodbye...Doctor."

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:46.439
Dr. Sun gave him a nod in return, then turned
and left SCP-049's cell for the last time.

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:52.510
The next day, SCP-049 was moved to a secure
transport vehicle, and driven to a nondescript

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:54.769
cemetery near Joppa, Indiana.

00:03:54.769 --> 00:03:59.849
There, operatives led him to the cave entrance
below, where it was sealed with concrete.

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:04.269
They brought with them tools to dismantle
the concrete seal, and additional concrete

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:08.959
to close the entrance back up once SCP-049
was inside.

00:04:08.959 --> 00:04:13.720
There would truly be no going back for the
Plague Doctor once he embarked on this last

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.629
great experiment.

00:04:15.629 --> 00:04:20.509
Once the way was cleared out, SCP-049 turned
to face his escorts.

00:04:20.509 --> 00:04:23.130
"Gentlemen, I thank you for your service.

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:28.710
I only hope that I may honor it by at last
defeating the Pestilence that threatens this

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:29.710
world."

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:33.169
Unsure of what to say in response, the officers
could only give him a silent salute.

00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:38.380
In the moment before he stepped over the threshold,
the Plague Doctor recalled a snippet of Shakespeare

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:41.980
he had once heard at the theatre, many many
years ago.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:47.120
He repeated it now: "Once more unto the breach,
dear friends, once more."

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.320
And he walked into the unknown.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:55.450
This strange new world was, at first, indistinguishable
from the old one that the Doctor had left

00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:56.450
behind.

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:02.610
It was just as the file had said, everything
was identical, just entirely absent of life.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:07.639
That was the first detail the Plague Doctor
noticed, the dry vegetation poking up from

00:05:07.639 --> 00:05:08.639
the earth.

00:05:08.639 --> 00:05:14.240
Brown leaves curling from petrified tree branches,
pale grass parting the cracked dirt.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:19.550
The second detail to catch his attention was
the silence, deafening silence.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:24.590
Back at the Foundation Site, there was always
noise: the clatter of footsteps down the hall,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:31.009
pens scratching on clipboards, alarms blaring,
strange creatures wailing in the distance,

00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:32.240
D-Class screaming.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:36.330
Here, there was nothing, only the hollow whistle
of the wind.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:41.009
In this moment, as he stood at the top of
a hill staring out at a vast landscape of

00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:44.220
emptiness, the Plague Doctor felt doubt creeping
in.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:46.940
Had he made a mistake, coming to this place?

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:52.310
He had hoped to find knowledge here, had hoped
to unlock the secrets of the Pestilence, but

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:56.580
perhaps he had just consigned himself to a
lonely, eternal grave.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.650
But no!

00:05:57.650 --> 00:05:59.421
He shook away the feeling.

00:05:59.421 --> 00:06:04.449
There was no sense in becoming discouraged
so soon, when there was so much still to discover.

00:06:04.449 --> 00:06:08.389
He would explore the landscape and see what
surprises awaited.

00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:10.600
There would be time to despair later.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.410
And so, the Plague Doctor walked.

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:17.199
He walked past fields of cattle lying on their
sides, so undisturbed they almost appeared

00:06:17.199 --> 00:06:21.099
to be sleeping if it weren't for their complete
and utter stillness.

00:06:21.099 --> 00:06:25.979
The lack of decomposition gave him pause,
as he realized that microbial life must have

00:06:25.979 --> 00:06:29.289
been eliminated by this world's Great Dying
as well.

00:06:29.289 --> 00:06:33.440
He stepped around broken birds where they
had fallen clear out of the sky and landed

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:38.280
on the ground, and looked pitifully at the
cars parked on the side of the road with long-dead

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.300
drivers still inside.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:44.169
The world, just as it was at the moment of
collective death.

00:06:44.169 --> 00:06:47.509
It was as fascinating as it was tragic.

00:06:47.509 --> 00:06:52.230
After a long walk through the infinite graveyard,
the Doctor saw a building up ahead that piqued

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:57.300
his interest: a hospital left abandoned, windows
caked with dust.

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.870
He couldn't be sure what he hoped to find
inside, but a building filled with medical

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:06.710
equipment, and possibly beds filled with deceased
patients to examine, would be an excellent

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:08.940
place to start.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.430
SCP-049 wandered the halls of the hospital,
gathering supplies as he went and placing

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.660
them into his trusty black bag.

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:21.610
He was admiring an IV stand when he heard
something curious: a metallic clank, coming

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.090
from down the hall.

00:07:23.090 --> 00:07:27.760
It was notable, not only because the building
appeared so empty, but because it was the

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:33.910
first sound he had heard since stepping into
the cave and leaving his world behind.

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:34.910
Could it be?

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:38.180
Could something else be alive in this place
after all?

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:43.980
He followed the sound eagerly to its source,
an operating room at the end of the hallway.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:49.319
He opened the door, and came face to face
with the last thing he ever expected to see:

00:07:49.319 --> 00:07:50.419
himself.

00:07:50.419 --> 00:07:55.840
This figure was slightly different, wearing
a deep red mask instead of the Doctor's signature

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:56.840
white.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:08:01.870
But everything else was the same, from the
gloved hands, to the robes, to the beak, to

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.150
the bag of implements and samples at his feet.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:10.800
The red-masked doctor regarded him with a
pleasant curiosity as they locked eyes.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:12.009
"Hello, Doctor."

00:08:12.009 --> 00:08:13.009
"Hello.

00:08:13.009 --> 00:08:16.520
I must ask, my dear fellow...are you me?"

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:19.449
"I do believe I must be."

00:08:19.449 --> 00:08:21.240
The red-masked doctor said simply.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:24.710
"I have never seen anyone else like you before.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:25.710
Like us.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:27.159
Where did you come from?"

00:08:27.159 --> 00:08:29.550
"From a world much like this one."

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:30.879
The Doctor explained.

00:08:30.879 --> 00:08:36.130
He went on to tell his double the entire story,
from his capture by the Foundation, to his

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:42.130
discovery of the SCP-2935 file, every step
of the journey that brought him to this very

00:08:42.130 --> 00:08:43.130
place.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:49.380
"I had hoped to conduct research and discover
enough to fill my solitude, but with you here..."

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.360
His imagination brimmed with possibilities.

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:56.660
"You could tell me, if you will, what happened
to reduce the world to this state?"

00:08:56.660 --> 00:09:01.630
"The necessary cost of scientific advancement
is what happened."

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.380
The red-masked doctor responded.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:07.370
"Collateral damage, as is to be expected in
any great endeavor."

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.180
"What do you mean?"

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.180
The Doctor frowned.

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:12.750
"The Pestilence did this, surely?"

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.579
"In a sense."

00:09:14.579 --> 00:09:17.300
The red-masked doctor's eyes glittered behind
his mask.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:22.610
"As my work progressed, this result became...unavoidable,
you see.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.670
It was the only way to cure them.

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:29.400
One must purge the poison entirely, if no
other solution can be found."

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.810
"Do you mean to tell me..."

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:34.300
The Plague Doctor struggled to find the words.

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:36.080
"That you did this?"

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.290
"Do not look so shocked, new friend."

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.310
The red-masked doctor scoffed.

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:44.630
"If we are alike, then you certainly must
have sacrificed a great deal to the pursuit

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:45.630
of a cure.

00:09:45.630 --> 00:09:47.800
It is for the greater good, yes?"

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:52.150
"Yes, I suppose I have...but not like this.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:53.730
Never like this."

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:54.730
He shook his head.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:58.519
"What are we, as doctors, with no more patients
to treat?"

00:09:58.519 --> 00:09:59.519
"Free."

00:09:59.519 --> 00:10:00.770
The red-masked doctor smiled.

00:10:00.770 --> 00:10:02.520
"No, no, no."

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:04.320
The Doctor could not believe what he was hearing.

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:05.990
"What of your world?"

00:10:05.990 --> 00:10:07.170
His twin demanded.

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:09.019
"What became of the patients there?"

00:10:09.019 --> 00:10:12.100
"I left them behind, in search of my cure
here."

00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:13.250
The Doctor retorted.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.940
The red masked figure paused thoughtfully.

00:10:15.940 --> 00:10:18.810
"They are all...still there?

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:21.020
On the other side of this SCP-2935?

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:25.670
Where did you say the entrance was, my friend?"

00:10:25.670 --> 00:10:27.990
"I neglected to mention it.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.329
And I never will.

00:10:29.329 --> 00:10:32.380
You will not go back through that gateway!"

00:10:32.380 --> 00:10:35.510
The Doctor backed away from the red-masked
man in horror.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:39.889
This figure looked like him, but he was villainous,
cold, and cruel.

00:10:39.889 --> 00:10:41.220
"No matter.

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.760
I will go to Site 19 and find the file myself.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.240
After all, I have all the time in the world."

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:51.050
The red masked doctor swept out of the room,
leaving SCP-049 stunned.

00:10:51.050 --> 00:10:56.350
If the other Doctor discovered the location
of that gateway, if he returned to the other

00:10:56.350 --> 00:11:00.910
world...the same terrible fate would befall
every living thing there.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:05.090
It was his duty as a Doctor to ensure that
did not happen.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:09.089
As fast as his legs could carry him, the Doctor
raced to Site-19.

00:11:09.089 --> 00:11:10.959
He only hoped he would not be too late.

00:11:10.959 --> 00:11:15.829
At the abandoned Foundation Site, the Plague
Doctor tore through the halls searching for

00:11:15.829 --> 00:11:20.000
a hint of movement, for a glint of red that
might lead him to his wicked other.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.760
If he could not find him...there was another
way.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:28.329
He dimly recalled overhearing the location
of an emergency switch, only to be flipped

00:11:28.329 --> 00:11:31.970
in the most dire of circumstances when all
else was lost.

00:11:31.970 --> 00:11:35.880
Now was the time for such a switch, the Plague
Doctor knew.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.260
Just as he had the switch in his sights, the
Plague Doctor heard a voice behind him.

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.010
"You will not stop me.

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.620
Why not join me?

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:47.050
We could be colleagues, battling the Pestilence
together."

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.560
The red masked doctor held out a hand in invitation.

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:53.610
"You are as foul a plague as the Pestilence
itself."

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:54.970
The Plague Doctor hissed.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:59.070
"Then I will leave you here alone."

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.760
The red masked doctor spat.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:03.190
"Neither you nor I will ever leave this place.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:04.680
I will make sure of it."

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:08.450
The Plague Doctor reached for the switch as
the realization dawned on the other doctor's

00:12:08.450 --> 00:12:09.450
face.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:13.250
The red-masked Doctor lunged desperately at
his counterpart, but it was too late: the

00:12:13.250 --> 00:12:16.600
Plague Doctor flipped the switch, and the
countdown began.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:19.450
The on-site nuclear warhead was preparing
to detonate.

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:20.720
"You fool!"

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.040
The red masked doctor hissed.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:24.040
"This will kill us both!"

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:27.770
"It may, but on the other side of that great
divide, they shall live."

00:12:27.770 --> 00:12:29.029
The Plague Doctor replied.

00:12:29.029 --> 00:12:31.230
"The Pestilence will take them all!"

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.660
The Plague Doctor shook his head.

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:33.960
"Perhaps you are right.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:37.610
But I believe they will find a way to fight.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:41.260
You and I will not get the chance to see who
is correct, I fear.

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:43.640
But I have made my peace with that."

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:45.760
"You have ruined everything!"

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:49.510
The red-masked doctor insisted, but the Plague
Doctor did not hear.

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:52.140
He was already closing his eyes, listening
to the countdown.

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:53.200
"Once more..."

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.760
He murmured to himself.

00:12:54.760 --> 00:12:56.870
"Unto the breach..."

00:12:56.870 --> 00:13:00.779
The tinny voice over the speakers counted
down: "3...2...1..."

00:13:00.779 --> 00:13:06.680
Now go check out “SCP-049 Cures SCP-096
of the Pestilence?!”

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:10.000
and “SCP-049 - What Actually is the Pestilence?

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.740
The Plague Doctor Questions and Theories”
for more Plague Doctor!

